ry point on the surface.\n\n- On the other hand, $r$ and $z$ can vary arbitrarily in their respective domains.\n\nTherefore, the equation of the surface in cylindrical polar coordinates is $\\theta =\\frac{11\\pi }{8}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298636 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eae7e5be-e883-5658-84a0-5de5da567887" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Polar Equation of a Given Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17b987a6-5614-5489-97f6-59db7f322d3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta =-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298638} {:answer/id #uuid "3353c913-7524-57b0-84d5-349976b4f606" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=-r" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298639} {:answer/id #uuid "5c93c71a-91c1-50eb-be6a-bc7ce91ffb27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=-\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298640} {:answer/id #uuid "13b3c2c3-3ac7-5ca2-8d25-1c33f957eae9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298641} {:answer/id #uuid "65134617-7665-5723-8acd-824015609587" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298642}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13b3c2c3-3ac7-5ca2-8d25-1c33f957eae9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298641} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1f5803b-1624-5343-8b47-69620b5dc82e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298637}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5aaf6f02-fb79-5723-9bea-f3492c611351" :question/math-academy-id "q-104213" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038052/assets/fe283d8f0d0b78729a7fc7bda93e900e1f310de2dbbc62f23d8f8a7ff65af462.p